Instruments whose initialization fails are now closed right away, so that the resources they
acquired before the failure, such as an open VISA connection, are freed immediately rather than
when the instrument is garbage collected. Previously, retrying to create an instrument for a
resource that can only be opened once could fail until the garbage collector had run.
This also applies to instruments that cannot be registered, e.g. because their name is already in
use, or that have abstract parameters, and to instruments whose ``__init__`` returns a value (which
raises a ``TypeError``).
If closing the instrument fails too, this is added as a note to the error of the initialization.
Instruments that fail before ``Instrument.__init__`` has completed, e.g. because a driver validates
its arguments first, are not closed, since close methods rely on the name, parameters and logger
that it sets up.
